// zoomwin.cla: gated UI scenario (window-zoom-hscroll Task 1) -- zoom box
// end to end: snap the 300x200 window (S1), `zoom` out to the standard
// state (full screen minus menu bar; fires `resized`, S2), `zoom` back in
// (ZoomWindow restores the saved userState; fires `resized` again, S3).
// The Go test asserts S2 differs from S1 and S3 is byte-identical to S1
// (geometry round-trips), on top of the golden compares.
//
// zoomwin.events opens with `menu 0 0` (a well-defined MenuSelect-style
// no-op: menuID 0 means "nothing selected", rt_ui_menu_dispatch returns
// immediately) purely to force the harness's post-verb event pump before
// the first `snap` -- otherwise S1 captures the screen before the window's
// very first update event has been processed at all (no scenario before
// this one opened with `snap` as its literal first verb; existing ones
// that snap early use a leading `tick` instead, which is unsuitable here:
// tick's TEIdle call toggles the focused textview's caret blink, and since
// zoom's own ZoomWindow animation eats enough real time to toggle it again,
// a `tick`-primed S1 and the post-zoom S3 land on opposite blink phases and
// never compare byte-equal even though the geometry genuinely round-trips).

window Panel {
    title: "Zoom"
    size: 300, 200
    resizable: min(200, 120)

    textview Body { at: 10, 10; fill: both; scrollbar: vertical }
}

on App.launch {
    open Panel
}
